{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E8ChAju6CXirZmWnx4iPod","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/thim/.claude/plans/plan-how-you-would-buzzing-pascal.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7892de3-ffd3-4dec-a961-da8c356db8b9","uuid":"e7d85c2b-02a4-48ff-bbee-cf5f590684ad","timestamp":"2026-09-18T21:22:08.168Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/thim/.claude/plans/plan-how-you-would-buzzing-pascal.md","content":"# Plan: add a `--version` flag to the Go CLI\n\n## Context\n\nThe repo is a single-file Go program (`main.go`, module `fixture`, `go 1.22`) that prints\n`hello`. It has no flag parsing, tests, Makefile, CI, or git tags. The goal is to make\n`./fixture --version` print a version string and exit 0, without changing the existing\ndefault behaviour (`./fixture` still prints `hello`).\n\n## Approach\n\nUse only the standard library (`flag` and `runtime/debug`). No new dependencies.\n\n1. **Add a package-level `version` variable** in `main.go`:\n   ```go\n   var version = \"dev\"\n   ```\n   Release builds override it with\n   `go build -ldflags \"-X main.version=v1.2.3\"`.\n\n2. **Resolve a fallback from build info** when `version` is still `\"dev\"`: read\n   `debug.ReadBuildInfo()` and use `info.Main.Version` if it is set and not `\"(devel)\"`.\n   This makes `go install fixture@vX.Y.Z` report the right version with no ldflags.\n\n3. **Register the flag** with the standard `flag` package in `main()`:\n   ```go\n   showVersion := flag.Bool(\"version\", false, \"print version and exit\")\n   flag.Parse()\n   if *showVersion {\n       fmt.Println(\"fixture \" + resolvedVersion())\n       return\n   }\n   fmt.Println(\"hello\")\n   ```\n   Go's `flag` accepts both `-version` and `--version`, so no extra handling is needed.\n\n4. **Keep the existing output untouched**: `hello` still prints when no flag is given.\n\n## Files\n\n- `main.go` — the only file to modify (add `flag`/`runtime/debug` imports, `version`\n  var, `resolvedVersion()` helper, flag handling in `main`).\n- `main_test.go` — new. One test for `resolvedVersion()` covering the ldflags-set case\n  (set `version = \"v9.9.9\"` and assert the result) and the default `\"dev\"` case.\n\nNo changes to `go.mod` (stdlib only).\n\n## Verification\n\n```sh\ngo vet ./... && go test ./...\ngo build -o fixture .\n./fixture                                   # prints: hello\n./fixture --version                         # prints: fixture dev\n./fixture -version                          # same\ngo build -ldflags \"-X main.version=v1.2.3\" -o fixture . && ./fixture --version\n                                            # prints: fixture v1.2.3\n./fixture --version; echo $?                # exit code 0\n```\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
